 To simplify the radical $\sqrt{2940}$, we first look for a perfect square factor in the radicand (2940). We notice that 100 is a perfect square and is a factor of 2940.

$$ \begin{aligned} \\ \sqrt{2940} & = \sqrt{100 \cdot 29.4} \ \sqrt{29.4} &\text{[Take the perfect square out, so we have the remaining factor]}

\end{aligned}

$$

Now, we can simplify the square root of 29.4. However, since 29.4 is not a perfect square, we can express it as a product of a perfect square and another number.

$$ \begin{aligned} \\ \sqrt{29.4} & = \sqrt{0.25 \cdot 117.6} \ \sqrt{117.6} &\text{[Take the perfect square out, so we have the remaining factor]}

\end{aligned}

$$

Again, 117.6 is not a perfect square, but it can be expressed as a product of a smaller perfect square and another number.

$$ \begin{aligned} \\ \sqrt{117.6} & = \sqrt{1.44 \cdot 82} \ 3.96 &\text{[Take the perfect square out, so we have the remaining factor]}

\end{aligned}

$$

Therefore, the simplified form of $\sqrt{2940}$ is $3.96\sqrt{82}$.

